# Shrek Onion policy — which signed layers belong on THIS machine (docs/phase4-oniond.md).
#
# oniond merges ONLY the layers listed here, and ONLY if they also pass the baked signature/verity
# gate (systemd-sysext --image-policy). A layer present on the store but not listed is
# "signed-but-omitted"; a listed layer that fails the trust gate is refused. This file is sealed
# under dm-verity in the image, so the selection itself is trusted — it is never read from the
# untrusted layer store.
#
# Format: `enable <layer-name>` (the DDI's basename without .raw). `#` comments and blanks ignored.
enable shrek-hello
enable shrek-conf
# Desktop Bootstrap-0: the Rung-2 Wayland desktop runtime (Sway + Qt6 QML + Quickshell), delivered as
# the signed shrek-desktop sysext (scripts/build-desktop-layer.sh). Sealed-enabled here so oniond
# proposes it and the gatekeeperd broker merges it onto /usr; the shrek-desktop-gate.service then
# proves the shell surfaces instantiate headless in the sealed boot (Pn-desktop). docs/desktop-bootstrap-0.md.
enable shrek-desktop
